	"title"		"Sort to nearby chests"
	"changenote"		"v1.1.0: new setting ControllerButton: choose which controller button sorts (LT, RT, pressing the left or right stick, or none)"
	"description"		"Tired of emptying your bag chest by chest?
One click puts your items into the chests around you that already hold the same items.

[img]https://community.fastly.steamstatic.com/public/images/sharedfiles/rate_ico_up_bright.png[/img] [b]Enjoying the mod? Please give it a thumbs up![/b] It helps other players find it.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]One-click sorting[/b] from the inventory screen (Character tab), with mouse or controller
[*][b]Items go where they belong:[/b] into chests that already contain that item, or into storages made for it (like firewood sheds)
[*][b]Keeps what you need:[/b] tools, hotbar items, the seed in your hand, faith, bags and quest items stay with you
[*][b]Sort a bag:[/b] open a bag and sort, and only that bag's contents go into the chests
[*][b]Works like the game:[/b] the button looks and behaves like the game's own move-all button, and items are moved the same way the chest window moves them
[*][b]Translated[/b] into all the game's languages
[/list]

[h2]How to use[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Mouse:[/b] click the button on the right of the Inventory header (with a bag open: on the bag's header)
[*][b]Controller:[/b] press [b]LT[/b] on the Character page; the prompt is shown at the end of the tip bar (RT or pressing a stick can be chosen in the settings)
[/list]
The button turns grey when there is nothing to sort or no chest nearby.
With a bag open, only that bag is sorted. Otherwise only your inventory is sorted and bags keep their contents.

[h2]What gets sorted[/h2]
[list]
[*]Inside a storage area (home, kitchen, yard...): that area's storages, the same ones the inventory screen lists
[*]Outside an area: storages within 10 units (adjustable)
[*]Items no nearby chest contains yet stay with you, and so does whatever doesn't fit. Turn on [i]OverflowToOtherChests[/i] to put them into any nearby chest with room
[*]Conveyor chests and pallets are skipped by default
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]Tested with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3806668942]No More Running Back[/url], [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3809616755]Performance Fixes[/url], Better Auto Crafting and GK2 Move Stations
[*]No More Running Back is optional; with it, its controller prompts are kept as they are
[/list]

[h2]Safety[/h2]
[list]
[*]Adds no data of its own to save files; add or remove it at any time
[*]If a game update breaks something, the mod switches itself off and the game runs as normal
[/list]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases/latest]BepInEx 5[/url]
[*]No other mods needed
[/list]

[h2]Install[/h2]
[b]Workshop:[/b] subscribe; with the GK2 Workshop auto-loader installed, it loads on the next game start

[b]Manual:[/b] copy the [i]BepInEx[/i] folder from
[code]steamapps\workshop\content\4358690\3809824680[/code]
into the game folder (Steam Library → right-click Graveyard Keeper 2 → Manage → Browse local files); merge the folders

Game folder after a manual install:
[code]
Graveyard Keeper 2
└─ BepInEx
   └─ plugins
      └─ GK2SortToNearbyChests
         └─ GK2SortToNearbyChests.dll   ← new
[/code]

[h2]Settings[/h2]
[list]
[*][i]BepInEx\config\gk2.sorttonearbychests.cfg[/i] is created on first start
[*]Choose what stays in your inventory, the search radius, overflow and conveyor use, and the controller button (LT, RT, LStick, RStick or None)
[/list]

[h2]Uninstall[/h2]
Unsubscribe, and delete [i]BepInEx\plugins\GK2SortToNearbyChests[/i] if you installed manually.

